<title>USA: BHC Comms Q2 net rises including pretax gain.</title>
<headline>BHC Comms Q2 net rises including pretax gain.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>BHC Communications Inc</p>
<p>				    Second Quarter     Six Months</p>
<p>				  1997	1996	1997	1996</p>
<p> Operating revenues    $118,835  $120,920  $219,953  $221,965</p>
<p> Operating income	  33,581    36,601    51,073    55,794</p>
<p>Other income (expense):</p>
<p>Gain on change of ownership</p>
<p>   in UPN, net		    -	   -   152,224	   -</p>
<p>Equity in United Paramount</p>
<p>   Network loss (a)    (16,404)  (34,990)  (34,302)  (67,744)</p>
<p>				  4,228  (14,969)   158,562  (25,241)</p>
<p>Income before income taxes and</p>
<p>     minority interest   37,809    21,632   209,635    30,553</p>
<p> Net income		  17,418     5,669   116,908     6,747</p>
<p> Net income per share	 .74	 .24	4.97	 .28</p>
<p> Avg shrs (b)		23,399    24,025    23,529    24,106</p>
<p>		  (In thousands except per share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) BHC owned UPN from its 1994 inception through January 15, 1997, when Viacom Inc exercised an option to buy half of UPN. BHC continues to account for its interest in UPN under the equity method.</p>
<p>(b) The decline in average common shares outstanding reflects purchases by BHC of its Class A common shares.</p>
<p>Q2 net income includes a $152,224,000 pretax gain on Viacom's acquisition of UPN stake and resulting reduction in the amount of UPN start-up losses recorded by BHC.</p>
</text>
